.TH CWE-191 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-191 \- Integer Underflow (Wrap or Wraparound)
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product subtracts one value from another, such that the result is less than the minimum allowable integer value, which produces a value that is not equal to the correct result. This can happen in signed and unsigned cases.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB2\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2014\-0497
Adobe Flash Player, added 2024\-09\-17.
.PP
Adobe Flash Player Integer Underflow Vulnerablity.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Adobe Flash Player contains an integer underflow vulnerability that allows a remote attacker to execute arbitrary code.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
The impacted product is end\-of\-life (EoL) and/or end\-of\-service (EoS). Users should discontinue utilization of the product.
 Due 2024\-10\-08.
.PP
